his change, starting from the beginning of July, the MTA deployment will switch the default value for the buildpack parameter from sap_java_buildpack (SAP Java Buildpack 1) to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta (SAP Java Buildpack 2).  Action:  Plan and migrate your applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 ahead of the scheduled change. In your deployment descriptors, you need to explicitly set one of the parameters buildpack or buildpacks of the java, java.tomcat, and java.tomee modules to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta. Note that this transition involves more than just configuration updates and may require code modifications.  See:  Migrate your Applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2  SAP Java Buildpack 2: Jakarta-Based, Fresh and New!  TomEE 10 has landed in SAP Java Buildpack 2!  \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-12\nValid as Of: 2025-06-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 650 ---\nComponent: Cloud Logging\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Upcoming OpenSearch Stack Update\nDescription: Heads-Up: Cloud Logging will upgrade its underlying OpenSearch stack from OpenSearch 1.3 to OpenSearch 2.19. The upgrade will be done in a phased approach allowing for an extensive preview/exploration phase before the eventual forced upgrade.  Action Required: For most instances, there should be no changes. However, you might be affected if you are using anything of the following:      mapping types in your custom indices  Destination API to manage destinations  Wildcard queries against text fields with the option case_insensitive:false      For detailed guidance on how to address these cases and the timelines for the phased rollout, see SAP Note 3617458 .  In case you build dashboards on your own: we noticed a few minor UI glitches (such as text wrapping, sizing, alignment difference). We will publish guidance on how to adapt the dashboards in early Q3, 2025.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-12\nValid as Of: 2025-06-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",2632\n465,\" subaccount display name, subaccount ID, and/or subdomain name. Joule validates the name you enter and provides suggestions should it not recognize your entry.  Entities and attributes:  Cloud Foundry Space: ID name, space name  Global Account: subdomain, display name  User: email address  Role Collection: name  Region: region (technical name), display name  Subaccount: ID, display name, subdomain  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 870 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Removal of SAP Java Buildpack 1\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been deprecated and will be removed from SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on June 30, 2025. As a consequence, deployments of MTAs containing modules of type java, java.tomcat, and java.tomee might start to fail, as the buildpack used by default is SAP Java Buildpack 1.   To ensure compliance with this change, starting from the beginning of July, the MTA deployment will switch the default value for the buildpack parameter from sap_java_buildpack (SAP Java Buildpack 1) to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta (SAP Java Buildpack 2).  Action:  Plan and migrate your applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2 ahead of the scheduled change. In your deployment descriptors, you need to explicitly set one of the parameters buildpack or buildpacks of the java, java.tomcat, and java.tomee modules to sap_java_buildpack_jakarta. Note that this transition involves more than just configuration updates and may require code modifications.  See:  Migrate your Applications to SAP Java Buildpack 2  SAP Java Buildpack 2: Jakarta-Based, Fresh and New!  TomEE 10 has landed in SAP Java Buildpack 2!  \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n\",1333\n120,\"--- Record 1341 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Link to the Task in Email Notification\nDescription: Email notifications now include task details and a direct action link. Click the link to complete tasks directly in My Inbox or SAP Task Center. See Manage and Personalize your Notifications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-24\nValid as Of: 2025-02-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1342 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Service Center\nDescription: You can now add an OData service to a Java project from the Service Center. See Service Actions for Development.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-23\nValid as Of: 2025-02-23\nVersion: T2501b\n\n--- Record 1343 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enrichment Data API - Decommissioning of the Endpoint: Delete Enrichment Data (Synchronous)\nDescription: The Enrichment Data API endpoint Delete Enrichment Data (Synchronous) is now decommissioned and is no longer available.  Please use the endpoint Delete Enrichment Data to delete data records.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-20\nValid as Of: 2025-02-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1344 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Themes: SAP Belize Themes Were Deprecated\nDescription: The SAP Belize themes have been deprecated.   This is indicated next to the theme names in the runtime site under Settings  Appearance  Theme.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLates